## Installing

Release builds come in four files, all named after the version:

- `hinge-<version>-win-x64-setup.exe` installs for the current user, with
  Start menu and desktop shortcuts, and lets you pick the folder.
- `hinge-<version>-win-x64-portable.exe` runs without installing.
- `hinge-<version>-linux-x86_64.AppImage` runs as is once marked executable.
- `hinge-<version>-linux-amd64.deb` installs with `sudo apt install ./<file>`.

The builds are not code signed, so Windows SmartScreen asks before the
first run. Each one bundles its own `adb`; an adb server that is already
running is used as it is.

## Development setup

From a checkout of this repository:

```sh
npm install
npm run fetch-vendor
```

`fetch-vendor` downloads and checksums the bundled `adb` (Android platform-tools
r37.0.1) and `scrcpy-server-v4.1` into `vendor/` (gitignored). Pass `--only win` or
`--only linux` to fetch one platform.
